<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Best in Slot Gear list for Enhancement Shaman DPS in Cataclysm Classic Pre-Raid. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from dungeons, reputations, and professions. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c7">Best in Slot Gear for Enhancement Shaman DPS in Pre-Raid</span></h2>Enhancement Shamans see a few major changes to itemization in Cataclysm: all DoTs can now crit and Agility is now the primary stat you will want to stack above all else with Attack and Spell Power being removed from most gear slots. Most importantly, Cataclysm brings armor specialization - which means that wearing all mail grants us 5% extra Agility through <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=86529/mail-specialization">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_chain_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mail Specialization</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>Overall, our primary gearing goals will be to stack Hit until the 17% Spell Hit cap (<b>~1742 rating</b>), get the 26 Expertise cap (<b>~781 rating</b>), and then go for our <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=77223/enhanced-elements">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_elementalprecision_2.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enhanced Elements</span></a> Mastery, a new stat which increases all Spell damage done by Enhancement <a class="icontiny c7" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=7/shaman">
<img alt="Shaman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_shaman.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shaman</span></a>s. Afterwards, Crit and Haste both have their upsides and downsides, but Crit is usually better, since crits proc <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=16282/flurry">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_ghoulfrenzy.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flurry</span></a> and thus give you a huge amount of baseline Haste you can count on. <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=51530/maelstrom-weapon">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shaman_maelstromweapon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Maelstrom Weapon</span></a> also quickens your casts massively, further lowering the value of Haste.<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Agility - This stat now gives Attack Power and also Spell Power through the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=30814/mental-quickness">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_mentalquickness.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mental Quickness</span></a> spec passive by itself, on top of the Dodge and Crit that it provided in WotLK. We mostly want to gem Agility, which is a red gem now.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Hit - The most efficient DPS stat until you hit the 17% Spell Hit cap.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Expertise - The second most efficient DPS stat until you hit the 6.5% Dodge removal cap.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Mastery - This is a new stat that directly increases your Spell Damage with an efficient rating to damage conversion.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Critical Strike - Crit is good for Enhancement due to the synergy with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=16282/flurry">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_ghoulfrenzy.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flurry</span></a>, but has a poor rating to 1% crit conversion.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Haste - Due to high baseline Haste from <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=16282/flurry">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_ghoulfrenzy.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flurry</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=51530/maelstrom-weapon">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shaman_maelstromweapon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Maelstrom Weapon</span></a>, Haste's contribution is not enough to make it a particularly good stat, although it also does not trail far behind the rest.</div></li></ol>
